  "notes": "ScopedReadSharesV1 (card T05). One allocation is lent to two children with complementary halves of the 1024-unit read authority; both borrowers read it while the parent also reads it, and the parent's writes sit on either side of the lending window because a write demands reconstructed exclusive authority. Three fixed Linux schedules run the case's own emitted C under ASan/UBSan/LSan with a heap witness that records every Buffer by address. The refusals this acceptance is the complement of are CT04 (write while a share is out) and CT05 (two FULL requests); they are mapped as their own cases rather than duplicated here. `proof` is unassessed: the nineteen QCore.ReadShare theorems constrain the model, not this fixture.",
